{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Vanessa and Marco's First Argument", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "My Way or the Highway", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 1, "type": "position"}, {"content": "scholar > Around the World > Jazzing it up in Montreal", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 12, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe  routines and regular activities in a wider range of social and work contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn6le12ob01re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Used to and Would to Talk About Past Habits", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you talk about repetitive events in the past, you can use <span class=\"strong\">used to</span> or <span class=\"strong\">would</span>.You usually use these expressions when you talk about memories from your childhood or earlier days.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Example:<br> I used to come visit here when I was a kid.<br>  We would come and visit my Uncle Doug - he lived here for ages.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">used to</span> when you refer to conditions, states or actions that do not happen anymore. <br><br><span class=\"italic\">Examples:<br> I used to have many friends at school.<br> My parents used to be strict with me.<br> We used to like the same type of music.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">would</span> for actions that were repetitive in the past. However, you do not use it to talk about past state. <br><br><span class=\"italic\">Example:<br> He would study for hours in the garden.<br> My mother would always tell me to not reveal too much at the start of a relationship.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use the infinitive verb with these expressions: <br>Used to + verb (I used to live here.) <br>Would + verb (We would talk for hours.)", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Rooms in a House", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "There are many different rooms in a typical North American house. Each room has its own purpose. Here is a list of rooms and some information about each. How are they different from rooms in your country?", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Look here in my study - I have a collection of snowglobes.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I bought new tools for my kitchen.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Where are you? I'm in the bedroom!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":8,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Room\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Purpose\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Living room\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A room where people come together to talk and watch TV.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Kitchen\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A room where people cook and sometimes eat meals. The kitchen is usually considered to to the \u201cheart\u201d of the home.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Dining room\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A room where people eat meals. It is usually for formal meals with guests.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Bathroom\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A room where people use the toilet, take showers/baths and wash their hands. There is usually more than one bathroom in a house.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Bedroom\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A room where people sleep and get dressed. There is usually more than one bedroom.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Den / Study\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A small room used for studying, reading or relaxing.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Laundry room\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A room where people wash and dry their clothes.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "anxiously", "type": "name"}, {"content": "wanting something very much", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm anxiously preparing for your visit.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le12ob01aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about people's behavior.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to await", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to wait for an event ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I've anxiously awaited your visit.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le12ob01aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "snow globe ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a toy that contains water and snow in a clear globe that creates a \u201csnowing\u201d scene when you shake it", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My uncle used to collect snow globes as souvenirs.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le12ob01aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to reveal ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to show", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Don't reveal too much at the beginning of the relationship.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le12ob01aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "study", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a small room to read or study in", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I keep my collection of snow globes in my study.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le12ob01aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "overly ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "excessively; unreasonably", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm overly sensitive today.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le12ob01aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Make a list of things that you used to do and things that you do now.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Compare your list with a partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Discuss the differences. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Ask follow-up questions to keep the conversation going.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I make a list of past and present habits.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share my list with my partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I ask follow-up questions to keep the conversation going.", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"exercises": [{"id": 0, "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Vocabulary and Grammar", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "I can talk about people's behavior and personality.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can talk about rooms and objects in them.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can talk about past and present habits.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "Where do you like to catch up with your friends?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "What do you like to do when you catch up with friends? </br>What do you talk about?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text